      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.38.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it was told to Tamar, saying, Behold, thy father-in-law goeth up to Timnath, to shear his sheep.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.38.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.38.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And she put off from her, her widow's garments, and covered her with a vail, and wrapped herself, and sat in an open place, which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by the way to Timnath: for she saw that Shelah was grown, and she was not given to him for a wife.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.38.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.38.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When Judah saw her, he thought her ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a harlot; because she had covered her face.",
